---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import Ring from '../../components/Ring.astro';
import { areaById } from '../../lib/areas';
import { getPaths, pathUrl, progress } from '../../lib/notes';
import { url } from '../../lib/site';

const paths = await getPaths();
---
<Base title="Learning paths" description="Four roadmaps: modern C++, system design, agentic engineering, and math foundations.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Learning paths</p>
    <h1>Four paths, one direction</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Each path is a sequence of stages and steps. Every step says what to learn, a practice project that makes it
      real, questions to check yourself, and the best resources. Notes you write attach to steps, so the path fills in
      as you go.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="grid grid-2">
    {paths.map((p) => {
      const pr = progress(p);
      const area = areaById(p.data.area)!;
      const started = pr.done + pr.doing > 0;
      return (
        <a class={`card path-card area-${p.data.area}`} href={pathUrl(p)}>
          <div class="top">
            <Ring pct={pr.pct} size={64} />
            <div>
              <span class="pill pill-area pill-dot">{area.name}</span>
              <h3 style="margin-top:0.35rem;font-size:1.4rem">{p.data.title}</h3>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="tagline">{p.data.tagline}</p>
          <p class="small muted" style="margin:0">{p.data.stages.length} stages · {pr.total} steps · {pr.done} done</p>
          <div class="stage-dots">
            {p.data.stages.map((s) => {
              const d = s.milestones.filter((m) => m.status === 'done').length;
              const g = s.milestones.some((m) => m.status !== 'todo');
              return <span class={d === s.milestones.length ? 'done' : g ? 'doing' : ''} title={s.title} />;
            })}
          </div>
          <div class="current">{started ? 'Up next' : 'Start here'}: <b>{pr.current.title}</b></div>
        </a>
      );
    })}
  </div>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>How the paths fit together</h2>
    <p>
      They're designed to reinforce each other. The C++ capstone (a small storage engine) is also a system design
      exercise. The math path's linear algebra and information theory make the transformer internals in the agentic
      engineering path readable. And the AI-era stage of system design is where everything meets: serving models,
      retrieval, and architecting agent systems.
    </p>
    <p>
      A good rhythm is one main path and one side path at a time. Move a step to <code>doing</code> when you start it
      and <code>done</code> when you can answer its check questions without notes. <a href={url('about/#how')}>How to update progress →</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
